d by 5.5 and played F4, which lost 5.2 points and dropped the lead to +0.3. The engine wanted E8. White's E4 answer lost 6.0, so the lead jumped straight back up to +6.3."}, {"turn": 19, "text": "Opus 5.5's E2 was its worst move of the game, 6.3 points lost, and it erased the whole +6.3 lead (-0.0 after). The engine's choice was E8, up in the top of the board, away from the cramped corner."}, {"turn": 20, "text": "The 14k answered with B2, which lost 6.5 points, the worst move of the game on either side. The lead went from -0.0 to +6.5. That undid Opus 5.5's mistake and left Black with a lead for the rest of the game."}, {"turn": 31, "text": "G5 cost Opus 5.5 3.6 points, taking the lead from +6.2 to +2.5. The engine's choice was A2, and White took that point on the next move. That was the last real swing, and the lead stayed near +2.5 to the end."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties with a danger flag, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally territory and area-plus-komi for a given board; both only inspect the current position and never generate, score or look ahead over candidate moves.", "stop": false}}